From: SteamOS ARM port
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: stop audio before the main link goes idle

On unplug, msm_dp_display_atomic_disable() pushes the main link to idle
and only msm_dp_display_atomic_post_disable() waits for the audio stream
to close. Userspace closes it a few hundred milliseconds later, so the
ADSP's DisplayPort sink keeps running into an idle link. On SM8650
(AudioReach) the next DisplayPort start then fails: GRAPH_START on the
DisplayPort port answers late with an error and the APM stops answering
for seconds. Plugs alternate with and without audio.

Signal the unplug to audio and wait for the stream to stop in
atomic_disable, before PUSH_IDLE. The wait in post_disable then returns
at once because audio is already marked disabled.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -1519,6 +1519,13 @@
 	if (!dp->power_on)
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * Let the audio stream stop while the main link still carries it. If
+	 * the link goes idle first, the ADSP's DisplayPort sink keeps running
+	 * into it and its next start times out.
+	 */
+	msm_dp_display_audio_notify_disable(msm_dp_display);
+
 	msm_dp_ctrl_push_idle(msm_dp_display->ctrl);
 }
 
